   "about": "Proficient in C, C++, Ada, and Python Programming Languages. Strong written and verbal communication skills. I have experience working closely with customers to define software requirements and test plans. I am a U.S. Citizen and have had security clearances in the past.\n\nI have extensive SW development experience with complex systems using C/C++, embedded SW, integration, processors, and various input/output devices. I have worked as a member of a number of different technical teams and I have good communication, and customer interface skills. \n\nI have experience testing and debugging software on target hardware in a lab environment. I have developed software drivers for hardware control and Built-In-Test on various embedded processor targets, including DSP's. I have experience working with Automatic Test Equipment communications busses such as Ethernet, MIL-STD-1553, RS-422, and analog/discrete IO. \n\nI am very good at generating and writing supporting documents such as test SW requirements, user manuals, software validation documents, etc. using MS Office suite applications (Word, Excel, Power Point, Microsoft Project). As a part of the software projects that I have worked on, I have contributed to the development of budgets, schedules, and proposals.\n\nI have extensive knowledge of aviation products as well as wireless hand-held devices and associated protocols.",
